 ludes an official Run for the Animals t-shirt and sponsor swag.\n\nThe 5K 
 course starts at Karst Farm Park and loops through the Monroe County Fairg
 rounds. The awards ceremony and sponsor booths are now located near the st
 art/finish line\, making it easier for participants and families to celebr
 ate together—and for faster results posting! After the awards\, stick ar
 ound for the raffles and fan-favorite pet contests! You don't have to be r
 egistered in the 5K to participate in the raffle and pet contests!\n\n**Ev
 ent Schedule:**\n\n**Sunday\, October 4**\n\n8:00 AM: Packet Pick-up & Ons
 ite Registration Opens\n\n9:15 AM: Registration Closes\, Trainer-led Group
  Stretch\n\n**9:30 AM: 5K Run Begins**\n\n**9:35 AM: 5K Walk Begins**\n\n1
 0:30 AM: 5K Run Awards Ceremony\n\n11:00 AM: Pet Contests & Raffle Winners
  Announced\n\nWe anticipate welcoming hundreds of runners\, walkers\, and 
 furry friends to this event! Don’t miss this great opportunity to suppor
 t animal welfare in our community!\n\nFor more information and to register
 \, visit ***monroehumane.org/5K.***
